+# Index file format, version 2
+
+All integers are little-endian. Offsets and sizes are in bytes.
+
+## Header (16 bytes)
+
+| Offset | Type | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | u32 | Magic `0x58444b50` ("PKDX") |
+| 4 | u16 | Version, 2 |
+| 6 | u16 | Reserved, 0 |
+| 8 | u32 | Record count |
+| 12 | u32 | String table size |
+
+## Records (24 bytes each)
+
+The records follow the header. The record block is count x 24 bytes. pkgdb refuses an index whose record block does not fit in 32 bits.
+
+| Offset | Type | Field |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0 | u32 | Name offset in the string table |
+| 4 | u16 | Name length |
+| 6 | u16 | Flags |
+| 8 | u32 | Path offset in the string table |
+| 12 | u16 | Path length |
+| 14 | u16 | Reserved, 0 |
+| 16 | u64 | Package size |
+
+## String table
+
+The string table follows the records. Names and paths are UTF-8 without a terminator. Each name and path must lie inside the table, or pkgdb refuses the index.
+
+## Changes from version 1
+
+- The record count is a u32 (a u16 in version 1), and the header has a reserved u16 before it.
+- Each record ends with the package size.
